@startuml poll-verify
' cumin works - the end of a run (I2): the checks after an Implementer run, the kept step after a temporary failure, and the way back to the Owner.
' Document: poll.md, sections on the end of a run and the way back to the Owner.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:The Implementer run ends;
if (Result?) then (done)
  repeat
    :Read the issue of the run again
    (one issue, the facts right after the run);
    :List the open pull requests of the branch
    that cumin chose (REST);
    backward :Keep the step (in memory).
    The issue stays in work, with its label.
    A poll 5 minutes later runs it again;
  repeat while (A call to GitHub of this step failed
  with a temporary failure? (a read, or
  the label change below)) is (yes) not (no)
  :Read the head commit of the worktree;
  partition "Decision (pure function, no I/O)" {
    if (An open pull request
    on the branch?) then (no)
      :failed: no open pull request;
    elseif (One by the bot of the
    Implementer App (<slug>[bot])?) then (no)
      :failed: another author;
    elseif (Head commit of the pull request
    equals the head of the worktree?) then (no)
      :failed: head commit not pushed;
    else (yes)
      :passed; add the link
      when the issue has none;
    endif
  }
  if (Passed?) then (yes)
    if (Add the link?) then (yes)
      :cumin-core adds the link
      (GraphQL addCloseIssueReferences);
      :Read the issue of the run again;
    endif
  endif
  if (Passed, and the link is there?) then (yes)
    :Change the label to cumin/status/awaiting-checks;
    stop
  else (no)
    :Build the comment
    (stop-note.md, one sentence for the failed check,
    or the answer of GitHub);
  endif
elseif (blocked) then
  :The comment is blocked_reason
  (decision-request.md, written by the agent);
else (abnormal end)
  :Retry, then hand it back to the Owner
  (the next implementation issue of this requirement);
  stop
endif

partition "Hand back to the Owner (the row number is an argument)" {
  :Comment on the implementation issue;
  :Change the label to cumin/status/awaiting-owner-decision;
  :Notify the Owner
  (the link is the comment; a setting can turn it off);
}
note right
  One failure does not stop the next step.
  Nothing is rolled back. Failures are logged.
end note
stop
@enduml
